</span><span style="background-color: var(--bg-secondary); display: block; white-space: pre; padding: 0px 20px;"><span class="linenumber react-syntax-highlighter-line-number" style="display: inline-block; min-width: 2.25em; padding-right: 1em; text-align: right; user-select: none; font-size: 11px; font-weight: normal; font-family: monospace; padding-left: 8px; color: rgb(0, 128, 0); font-style: italic;">171</span><span></span><span class="token list" style="color: rgb(57, 58, 52);">1.</span><span> (</span><span class="token" style="font-weight: bold; color: rgb(57, 58, 52);">**</span><span class="token content" style="font-weight: bold;">Token level</span><span class="token" style="font-weight: bold; color: rgb(57, 58, 52);">**</span><span>) Use a simple formula to calculate </span><span class="token code-snippet code" style="color: rgb(0, 0, 255);">`block table indices`</span><span>: </span><span class="token code-snippet code" style="color: rgb(0, 0, 255);">`request indices * K + positions / block size`</span><span>. So it equal to </span><span class="token code-snippet code" style="color: rgb(0, 0, 255);">`[0 * 6 + 0 / 2, 0 * 6 + 1 / 2, 0 * 6 + 2 / 2, 1 * 6 + 0 / 2, 1 * 6 + 1 / 2, 2 * 6 + 0 / 2, 2 * 6 + 1 / 2, 2 * 6 + 2 / 2, 2 * 6 + 3 / 2, 2 * 6 + 4 / 2] = [0, 0, 1, 6, 6, 12, 12, 13, 13, 14]`</span><span>. This could be used to select </span><span class="token code-snippet code" style="color: rgb(0, 0, 255);">`device block number`</span><span> from </span><span class="token code-snippet code" style="color: rgb(0, 0, 255);">`block table`</span><span>.
